      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__x430__types_1ga1618e2f9c05567bc41339e0fb98845b3" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>void(*</type>
        <definition>typedef void(* x430_read_hook) (struct x430_device *device, uint16_t address, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(struct x430_device *device, uint16_t address, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</argsstring>
        <name>x430_read_hook</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Data is about to be read (<ref refid="structx430__hooks_1aca48905169e4ee844638f12b46d3b0b6" kindref="member">x430_hooks::read</ref>). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Called once per contiguous run of real addresses (Indirect Data is resolved to the addresses it points at). The hook may refresh live registers with <ref refid="group__x430_1gaf7a2c5ffac2a155fd4c7afe4aa0cee8c" kindref="member">x430_device_set()</ref>. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>device</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device read. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>First real address of the run. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bytes in the run. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structx430__device__config_1a22187374bf1952dadb84ba9b9c4fd61d" kindref="member">x430_device_config::user_data</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/x430_types.h" line="134" column="9" bodyfile="inc/x430_types.h" bodystart="134" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__x430__types_1ga63594ce085fa44faa322668f28dfe54e" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>uint8_t(*</type>
        <definition>typedef uint8_t(* x430_event_hook) (struct x430_device *device, enum x430_event event, void *user_data)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(struct x430_device *device, enum x430_event event, void *user_data)</argsstring>
        <name>x430_event_hook</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Device event (<ref refid="structx430__hooks_1aa88bdb1b64a0a2e289c6de118f3a0c79" kindref="member">x430_hooks::event</ref>). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>device</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>event</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>What happened. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structx430__device__config_1a22187374bf1952dadb84ba9b9c4fd61d" kindref="member">x430_device_config::user_data</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>DXL2_ERR_NONE, or a DXL2_ERR_* code where the event can be refused (<ref refid="group__x430__defs_1gga7d5a16437bb5db3b961b2419ebe8f413a05b062231373da8ca6a8653c39051544" kindref="member">X430_EVENT_CLEAR_MULTI_TURN</ref>); ignored otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
