      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__x430__types_1ga9146fe322468686c662aa285ccba5aa7" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>int(*</type>
        <definition>typedef int(* x430_nvm_read_hook) (struct x430_device *device, enum x430_nvm_slot slot, uint16_t offset, uint8_t *data, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(struct x430_device *device, enum x430_nvm_slot slot, uint16_t offset, uint8_t *data, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</argsstring>
        <name>x430_nvm_read_hook</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Read part of a persistent block (<ref refid="structx430__hooks_1a5a7339c6c85d02ce552efd0088bb36aa" kindref="member">x430_hooks::nvm_read</ref>). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The device reads a block in parts, so that it needs no buffer of its own: first the whole block in chunks (header, payload and CRC are checked), then the registers it takes from it. Return the stored bytes; where they live is up to the application. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>device</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>slot</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Block to read. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>offset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>First byte, from the start of the block. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Destination of <computeroutput>length</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bytes; offset + length is at most <ref refid="group__x430__types_1ga7a4fa58fa1180c51322a90b3b0df9e5f" kindref="member">X430_NVM_EEPROM_SIZE</ref> or <ref refid="group__x430__types_1ga28c3665c1d2857bcfa630c5c4b5d708b" kindref="member">X430_NVM_BACKUP_SIZE</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structx430__device__config_1a22187374bf1952dadb84ba9b9c4fd61d" kindref="member">x430_device_config::user_data</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>0</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>length</computeroutput> bytes were read. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>&lt;0</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>No data: the device treats the block as missing (factory values stay). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/x430_types.h" line="164" column="9" bodyfile="inc/x430_types.h" bodystart="164" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group__x430__types_1gaa07179a5b4e38a94c05bac2880ecc738" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>int(*</type>
        <definition>typedef int(* x430_nvm_write_hook) (struct x430_device *device, enum x430_nvm_slot slot, uint16_t offset, const uint8_t *data, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(struct x430_device *device, enum x430_nvm_slot slot, uint16_t offset, const uint8_t *data, uint16_t length, void *user_data)</argsstring>
        <name>x430_nvm_write_hook</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Write part of a persistent block (<ref refid="structx430__hooks_1ad8b7dc1964e5ea54939219f0b5b8872e" kindref="member">x430_hooks::nvm_write</ref>), after the change; may be slow. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A block is written in parts with increasing offsets, from 0 to its end (<ref refid="group__x430__types_1ga7a4fa58fa1180c51322a90b3b0df9e5f" kindref="member">X430_NVM_EEPROM_SIZE</ref> or <ref refid="group__x430__types_1ga28c3665c1d2857bcfa630c5c4b5d708b" kindref="member">X430_NVM_BACKUP_SIZE</ref>): header, payload (straight from the Control Table image of the device) and CRC. Start a new block at offset 0 (for example erase the flash page) and commit it when offset + length reaches the size. A block that is not written to its end fails the CRC check when it is read. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>device</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>slot</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Block to write. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>offset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>First byte, from the start of the block. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>length</computeroutput> bytes, opaque to the application. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>user_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structx430__device__config_1a22187374bf1952dadb84ba9b9c4fd61d" kindref="member">x430_device_config::user_data</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>0</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Written. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>&lt;0</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Failure: the remaining parts are not written, the host gets Result Fail. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/x430_types.h" line="185" column="9" bodyfile="inc/x430_types.h" bodystart="185" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
